# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit the result.

# --- Required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Your Hudu instance. Origin only; /api/v1 is added by the client.
HUDU_BASE_URL=https://hudu.example.com

# Hudu Admin -> Basic Information -> API Keys.
#
# The key's scope is fixed at creation and cannot be changed afterwards, so
# create it with the least you need:
#   - password access      OFF, unless you intend to use HUDU_ALLOW_PASSWORD_REVEAL
#                          or HUDU_ALLOW_PASSWORD_WRITE
#   - destructive actions  OFF, unless you intend to use HUDU_ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE
#   - export capability    OFF, unless you intend to use HUDU_ALLOW_EXPORTS
#   - IP allowlist         set it, if the server has a stable address
#   - company scope        set it, if this key only needs one customer
#
# A key without password access is the strongest possible protection for your
# credential vault: no setting in this server can override what the key cannot do.
HUDU_API_KEY=replace-me

# --- Capability gates -------------------------------------------------------
# All default to off. Each one is an explicit decision by the operator, and no
# tool argument can turn any of them on.

# Register only Read tools. Nothing can write, delete, or archive.
# HUDU_READ_ONLY=1

# Register delete and purge tools, including the activity-log purge.
# HUDU_ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE=1

# Register hudu_reveal_password, which returns one stored secret at a time.
# Password metadata is available without this; only the secret values are withheld.
# HUDU_ALLOW_PASSWORD_REVEAL=1

# Register the password write tools: create, update, archive and delete a
# credential record. Separate from the reveal gate above, and neither implies
# the other — documenting a new credential without being able to read existing
# ones is a legitimate posture, and so is the reverse. Deleting a credential
# needs this and HUDU_ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE together.
# HUDU_ALLOW_PASSWORD_WRITE=1

# Register the bulk export tools. Note that this Hudu version offers no way to
# retrieve or track an export once started.
# HUDU_ALLOW_EXPORTS=1

# --- Pacing -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Hudu documents 300 requests/minute and documents no 429 response, so the
# client stays under the limit rather than reacting to being told it is over.

# HUDU_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=120
# HUDU_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4
# HUDU_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# HUDU_MAX_RETRIES=3

# --- Contract tests ---------------------------------------------------------
# Opt-in only. These run against the live instance above and make real calls.
# HUDU_CONTRACT_TESTS=1
